uding imported re-exports and submodules'","Plan: 'the value of pinned immutable constants (guards e.g. `prompts.FRONT_MATTER_KEYS`, `prompts.EXECUTION_MODES`)'","src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompts.py has no `__all__` (search returned no matches)","src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompts.py:89-91 re-exports FRONT_MATTER_KEYS from prompts_frontmatter; :50-52 re-exports EXECUTION_MODES from prompt_model — both via `X as X`, so their defining module is not `rebar.llm.prompting.prompts`","The plan's parenthetical 'the `rebar` facade and `rebar.signing`/`rebar.llm.workflow.executor` define one [__all__]' correctly omits prompts/runner/contracts/findings, confirming those four hit the no-__all__ branch"],"finding":"The plan's source-of-truth rule contradicts itself for prompts.FRONT_MATTER_KEYS / prompts.EXECUTION_MODES: rebar.llm.prompting.prompts defines NO __all__, so the rule falls to the 'members the module OWNS ... excluding imported re-exports' branch; but both constants are imported re-exports in prompts.py (`from rebar.llm.prompting.prompts_frontmatter import FRONT_MATTER_KEYS as FRONT_MATTER_KEYS`, `from rebar.llm.prompting.prompt_model import EXECUTION_MODES as EXECUTION_MODES`), i.e. exactly what the rule excludes — yet the plan names them as constants the baseline must guard.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc5d77defe7a9f3aa","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Source-of-truth rule (pinned)'","norm_id":"ne799d28adab43e3f","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer follows the rule literally: FRONT_MATTER_KEYS/EXECUTION_MODES are excluded as imported re-exports and never enter the baseline, silently dropping the subsumption coverage that the deleted test_reuse_surface_doc.py asserted (its lines 68-69).","Implementer relies on the 'module-level constant with no __module__' fallback to include them — but that fallback cannot distinguish an owned constant from an imported one (neither carries __module__)